# Xiaomi Mi Pad 3 vendor policy intentionally has no dex2oat rules.
# Android 12 declares `dex2oat` in system/sepolicy/private, so this BSP
# non_plat directory (compiled into vendor policy) cannot reference that type.
# The historical entries in this file were project-specific MTK exceptions:
# CIP access to /custom, an old execv diagnostic, and a K35V1 MTBF FD rule.
# They are not cappu requirements and caused checkpolicy to fail with
# "unknown type dex2oat". Keep the rationale here so these rules are not
# accidentally restored to vendor policy; any verified platform exception
# must be implemented in platform-private policy with compatible public labels.

